# Build output and dependencies.
#
# These patterns are ROOT-ANCHORED with a leading slash on purpose. An unanchored
# `build` matches a directory named `build` at ANY depth, which silently excluded
# four API routes that live at .../build/route.ts — the trade, create and claim
# transaction builders. They were missing from the repository and therefore from
# the deployed app, while still working locally. Keep the leading slash.
/node_modules
/.next
/out
/build
/coverage

# Environment — never commit real credentials.
.env
.env.local
.env*.local

# Tooling and OS noise.
.DS_Store
*.pem
*.tsbuildinfo
next-env.d.ts
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
/.vercel
